  "description_html": "<section aria-labelledby=\"courseDescription\">\n    Offered: Fall.\n\nPrerequisites:  AGAS 1014 and AGAS 2084, or consent of instructor. \n\nThis course is offered as a study in livestock selection according to desirable characteristics for cattle, swine, sheep, goats, and poultry. Evaluation criteria are presented according to industry standards for species&#39; breeds and expected market production. Students will be expected to develop safe handling practices with live animals.\n\n    \n</section>",
